SUMMARY:NEATwalks Step Back in Time: Learn about Toronto's Historical Landmarks at High Park
DESCRIPTION:Discover Toronto’s History – Colborne Lodge & the 1855 Coach House\nNeatwalks for newcomers to explore and appreciate Toronto! \nEvent Details:  \n\nFamily-friendly: Everyone is welcome! \nRain or shine: We’ll be there\, whatever the weather \nDress appropriately: Wear comfortable clothing and shoes suitable for the weather \nBring along: Water\, snacks\, and your camera to capture the memories\n\nMeeting Point:  \nQueensway and Colborne Lodge Drive (East side). Please arrive by 11:00 am sharp\, or earlier\, so you can join the official tour at the location. \nGetting There:\nFor the shortest walk to the meeting location\, take TTC Bus 80 from Keele. \nWho is for:  \nPermanent residents and Convention refugees (need to provide copy of immigration documents).   \nRegistration is required for the purpose of media and liability releases.  \nTo register:  \nFor new participants please fill this form   \nFor returning participants\, reserve your spot via text (437-249-7103) or email ( rchauhan@culturelink.ca)  \n 
URL:https://www.culturelink.ca/event/neatwalks-step-back-in-time-learn-about-torontos-historical-landmarks-at-high-park/
LOCATION:High Park\, 11 Colborne Lodge Drive\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M6S 5A3\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Families
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.culturelink.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Neat-Walks-Web-Icon.jpg
END:VEVENT
