SUMMARY:NEATwalks Stories in the Landscape: Indigenous Heritage and Fall Colors at High Park
DESCRIPTION:Neatwalks for newcomers to explore and appreciate Toronto!  \nLet Nature Lead:   \n\nTake a walk through Toronto’ iconic park with us! \n\n\nExplore how generations of Indigenous stewardship have shaped and sustained the remarkable Black Oak Savannahs\n\nMeeting Point: Arrive by 1:45 pm at the corner of High Park Blvd. at Bloor Street west.   \nWho is for: Permanent residents and Convention refugees (need to provide copy of immigration documents).  \nRegistration is required for the purpose of media and liability releases. \nTo register: For new participants please fill this form  \nFor returning participants\, reserve your spot via text (437-249-7103) or email ( rchauhan@culturelink.ca) 
URL:https://www.culturelink.ca/event/neatwalks-stories-in-the-landscape-indigenous-heritage-and-fall-colors-at-high-park/
LOCATION:High Park\, 11 Colborne Lodge Drive\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M6S 5A3\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Adults
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.culturelink.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Neat-Walks-Web-Icon.jpg
